# ───────────────────────────────────────────
# Skill-advisor runtime launcher state (transient build/launch records)
# ───────────────────────────────────────────
**/.mk-skill-advisor-launcher.json

# Deep-loop lineage runtime state. A dispatched CLI writes its own home here —
# sqlite databases, downloaded system skills, lock files, and potentially a linked
# credential. Regenerable, large, and a credential must never reach history or a
# cloud-sync client. The artifacts worth keeping sit beside it.
specs/**/lineages/*/.codex-home/

# Write-containment captures: the baseline copies a fan-out takes of files outside a lane, and
# the quarantine copies of a lane's stray writes. Per-run machine output. Tracked, they were
# copied into every later run's capture, nesting one level per run until paths outgrew the
# filesystem limit and a worktree could no longer be removed.
specs/**/containment/baseline/
specs/**/containment/quarantine/

# A packet-local save mutex, acquired by the continuity generator while it mutates
# canonical documents. It names the process holding it, so it is machine state and
# never belongs in history: a committed one outlives its process and describes an
# owner that no longer exists.
.canonical-save.lock/

# The HF model server's default state directory under the spec-kit runtime. It
# holds sockets, leases and logs for a machine-local process, so it is state
# rather than history.
.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/database/
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/database/

# The default output of sk-doc's frontmatter-version.mjs `compute` when no
# --manifest-out is given. It is run residue, rewritten on every run, and nothing
# reads it back unless it is passed explicitly with --from-manifest.
/frontmatter-version-manifest.csv
/frontmatter-version-manifest.json
